---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Predictive Analysis · Competitive Authority Stack · Yasser Gandhi Friction Scan"
  description="Three formal academic credentials from UNAM and UdeG translated into senior B2B competitive advantages: data extraction, cognitive scaffolding, resilient architecture design. 15 years of longitudinal proof."
  keywords="Friction Scan Consultant Credentials, User Retention Expert, Cognitive Scaffolding Software, Onboarding Architecture Expert, B2B Consulting Authority, Mexico City Tech Consultant, Software Churn Expert"
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section id="predictive-analysis">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-label">Competitive Authority Stack</div>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Predictive Analysis</h1>
        <p style="color: var(--gray); font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 640px;">
          Three Mexican SEP-certified degrees. Translated into international-grade competitive
          advantages for B2B software consulting.
        </p>
        <p style="color: var(--gray-dim); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 640px; font-family: var(--font-mono);">
          SEP Cédulas Profesionales: Verified credentials issued by Mexico's Secretaría de Educación
          Pública — the federal authority equivalent to a state bar or professional license in
          jurisdictions that require it.
        </p>

        <!-- Credential 01 -->
        <div class="project-card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <div class="project-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-production">Credential 01</span>
            <span class="badge badge-archived">B.A. Literature · UNAM</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Data Extraction & Break Detection</h2>
          <div class="project-body">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
              A formal degree in literary analysis from UNAM is not about books. It is about
              <strong style="color: var(--white-warm);">reading structural systems under compression</strong> —
              identifying the gaps between what a system claims to do and what it actually does,
              detecting inconsistencies that are invisible to automated scanners, and extracting
              meaning from signals that look like noise.
            </p>
            <p>
              Applied to software systems, this translates directly into
              <strong style="color: var(--white-warm);">friction archaeology:</strong>
              the ability to audit behavioral leaks, map invisible churn triggers, and identify
              where your onboarding logic breaks for real users under conditions your unit tests
              never simulate. Flat log analysis tells you a user left. This methodology tells
              you <em>why the architecture made them leave.</em>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="adr-quote">
            Trained formally to read between the lines. Deployed technically to audit the cracks
            in software onboarding flows that your analytics dashboard cannot see.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Credential 02 -->
        <div class="project-card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <div class="project-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-production">Credential 02</span>
            <span class="badge badge-archived">M.A. Pedagogy · UNAM</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Cognitive Scaffolding & System Onboarding</h2>
          <div class="project-body">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
              A Master's in Pedagogy from UNAM is not about classrooms. It is the
              <strong style="color: var(--white-warm);">exact scientific analysis of how human beings
              process new information, adopt complex tools, and build competence under pressure.</strong>
              The research field of cognitive scaffolding — building structured support systems that
              guide users toward independence — is the academic foundation of every effective
              onboarding architecture.
            </p>
            <p>
              When your user hits a wall in your activation flow, it is because the information
              sequencing violates how human cognition builds mental models. This credential provides
              the diagnostic framework to identify those violations with precision: which steps are
              cognitively overloaded, which UI patterns create unnecessary ambiguity, and which
              recovery paths reduce abandonment rather than accelerating it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="adr-quote">
            The science of how real users learn, adopt, and commit to software tools under real
            conditions — applied directly to your product's activation architecture.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Credential 03 -->
        <div class="project-card" style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
          <div class="project-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-production">Credential 03</span>
            <span class="badge badge-archived">B.Sc. Web Systems Dev. · UdeG</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Resilient Architecture Design</h2>
          <div class="project-body">
            <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
              GPA 98.5. A Bachelor of Science in Web Systems Development from the Universidad de
              Guadalajara is the technical foundation that converts behavioral diagnoses into
              <strong style="color: var(--white-warm);">executable engineering solutions.</strong>
              The friction is diagnosed. The architecture is designed. The fix is coded and deployed.
            </p>
            <p>
              This is not a consulting engagement that ends with a slide deck. The senior technical
              capability to build robust backend systems, clean data pipelines, enforce TypeScript/Zod
              contracts, and implement real-time fault mitigation means every recommendation comes
              with a proof of concept, a deployment strategy, and a measurable success criterion.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="adr-quote">
            The complete loop: diagnose friction → design the fix → build it → measure the result.
            No handoff to a separate engineering team required.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Longitudinal Proof -->
        <div style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
          <div class="section-label">The Longitudinal Proof</div>
          <h2>2011–2026: 15 Years of Uninterrupted Execution</h2>
          <p style="color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.95rem; max-width: 640px; line-height: 1.75;">
            Academic credentials establish the theoretical foundation. The longitudinal record
            establishes that the methodology has been stress-tested against real systems,
            real users, and real failure conditions — without interruption — for 15 years.
          </p>

          <div class="adr-timeline">
            <div class="adr-entry">
              <div class="adr-date">2011</div>
              <div class="adr-title">Origin: First Live Friction System</div>
              <div class="adr-desc">
                First deployment of a distributed user flow system under real high-friction
                conditions. Initial mapping of the gap between designed user behavior and
                actual user behavior.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="adr-entry">
              <div class="adr-date">2015–2020</div>
              <div class="adr-title">Academic Calibration Phase</div>
              <div class="adr-desc">
                Formal research at UNAM produced two peer-reviewed frameworks for cognitive
                scaffolding and behavioral analysis. Eleven Scopus-indexed contributions.
                Theoretical models validated against live user populations.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="adr-entry">
              <div class="adr-date">2022–2024</div>
              <div class="adr-title">Production-Grade System Engineering</div>
              <div class="adr-desc">
                B2C platform (huhugerman.com) deployed under real traffic with measurable
                friction diagnosis methodology. Domain-Driven Design, TypeScript contracts,
                Supabase/PostgreSQL — serving live users with documented behavioral data.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="adr-entry">
              <div class="adr-date">2025</div>
              <div class="adr-title">UdeG Degree Completed · GPA 98.5</div>
              <div class="adr-desc">
                Technical foundation formalized. Architecture decision records published.
                Full-stack capability certified.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="adr-entry dim">
              <div class="adr-date">2026 →</div>
              <div class="adr-title">Global B2B Friction Scan Consulting</div>
              <div class="adr-desc">
                The complete methodology available for B2B software teams who need to stop
                losing users to invisible friction in their onboarding and activation flows.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="text-align: center;">
          <a href="mailto:yassergandhi.dev@gmail.com?subject=Predictive%20Analysis%20Inquiry" class="btn-primary">
            [ Book a 15-Minute Friction Audit ]
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <hr class="divider" />
    <Contact />
  </main>
</Layout>
